<header><p class="enc-kicker">Place · city</p><h1 class="enc-title">Udupi</h1></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">Udupi is a city on the coast of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/karnataka">Karnataka</a>, south-western <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/india">India</a>, known for its <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/krishna">Krishna</a> temple and monasteries founded by the 13th-century philosopher <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/madhvacharya">Madhvacharya</a>, who was born nearby. It remains the main centre of the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/dvaita-vedanta">Dvaita</a> tradition and has given its name to a style of vegetarian cooking.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/udupi.jpg" alt="Udupi" width="320" height="214" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: (WT-en) Ravikiran Rao · CC BY-SA 4.0 · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Udupi_Krishna_Temple.jpg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
